# Windows/MSYS-specific ffmpeg flags. Layered on top of common/ffmpeg-features.

# Windows has the widest hardware coverage of any platform and all of it is
# free: d3d11va/d3d12va/dxva2 and MediaFoundation are OS APIs, and ffnvcodec
# (NVIDIA), amf (AMD) and vulkan are LoadLibrary-based. Nothing here adds an
# import beyond the system DLLs score already links (see
# score-plugin-media/CMakeLists.txt: evr, mf, mfplat, mfuuid, ...).
# Intel QSV is still absent: libvpl links for real.
--enable-dxva2
--enable-d3d11va
--enable-d3d12va
--enable-mediafoundation
--enable-ffnvcodec
--enable-nvdec
--enable-nvenc
--enable-cuvid
--enable-amf
--enable-vulkan

# schannel rather than openssl: it is a system SSP (-lsecur32 -lncrypt
# -lcrypt32), so there is no extra library to build or ship, it validates
# against the Windows certificate store users expect, and ffmpeg 9's
# tls_schannel.c implements DTLS *and* the SRTP keying-material export -- so
# https, rtmps and the whip muxer all work through it.
--enable-schannel
--disable-openssl
--disable-securetransport
--disable-videotoolbox

--disable-response-files
